  "source_revision": "f1945a2",
  "experimental_build": "opt-in CPU hot-path timers; bounded binding cache diagnostic; transfer-barrier and descriptor-write ablations were local only",
  "caveats": [
    "Concurrent runs across GPUs can cause host-noise; compare repeated same-GPU runs, not cross-GPU absolute times",
    "CUDA vs Vulkan GPU hardware differs; compute speed ranking cannot be inferred",
    "Optimizer-only excluded forward/backward and used GPU-resident static input gradients",
    "Eager shader timestamp totals differ from deferred wall-time and must not be subtracted as exact CPU cost",
    "Some temporary out= adapter measurements execute two shaders per API operation, not one",
    "The 8192 bound-algorithm cache experiment retained ~6400 entries and consumed more host memory; do not make the cache unlimited",
    "Bound descriptors and Vulkan resources must stay alive while command buffers are in flight."
  ],
